The '''Torre FDB''' is a 41-storey mixed-use office and residential tower at 200 Carrer Miquel in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. Completed in 1983, the tower was originally built as the headquarters of [[Banc de l'Estret]], a regional bank that expanded aggressively during the [[Balboa real-estate bubble|real-estate bubble]]. Following the bank's collapse in the [[Balboa real-estate asset crisis]] of 1988, the building was acquired at a significant discount by the [[Fons d'Inversió Directa de Balboa]] (FDB), which established its headquarters in the tower and converted the lower floors to residential use.

At 160 metres to its roof, 170 metres to its crown, and 190 metres to its antenna tip, the tower is one of the taller buildings in the Sant Cristòfor waterfront district. Its pale stone exterior contrasts strongly with the darker glass skyscrapers surrounding it, giving it a distinctive landmark presence on the skyline.

== Architecture ==

The Torre FDB is a late-modernist mixed-use high-rise with a strong corporate appearance softened by residential proportions. The tower has a tall, narrow rectangular form with a pale stone or precast-concrete exterior and a highly regular façade composed of repetitive window bays and shallow projecting frames.

The main tower rises from a broader, lower podium that contains the lobby, offices, retail space, parking, and building services. Above the podium, the shaft is divided into closely spaced vertical structural lines, while horizontal floor bands create a rigid grid across the façade. The many smaller windows and balcony-like recesses on the upper floors reflect the building's residential component, while the larger lower floors are suited to office use.

At the top, the building steps inward through several rooftop levels, creating a tiered crown. These upper sections contain mechanical equipment, communications facilities, and executive or amenity space. A tall striped antenna mast extends above the roof, making the tower more prominent on the skyline. Dark blue FDB signage is mounted on multiple sides of the crown for visibility from different directions.

